Performance bug found by profiling (cProfile, live fixture backend/tests/fixtures/upload/sam_video_upload_01.jsonl,
75 frames at 1280x960, 7.7 MB stream):
- meta-sam-parser decodes every mask's lossless raster in pure Python (_mask_codec._decode_lossless_raster, ~1-2.8 s
  per 1280x960 mask). It does it once at parse time to validate (_segmentation.py:480), and our sam.result_from_image
  then calls decode_mask_to_rle AND decode_mask_to_svg_path, and the SVG helper decodes again through
  decode_mask_to_rle. So each mask is decoded 3 times: parse_video_events alone took 108 s, and
  test_upload_fixtures.py::test_live_sam_video_stream_parses took 355 s. test_upload_video.py hangs for minutes too, and
  test_vision_parse.py (41 s) / test_vision_routes.py (25 s) are slow for the same reason. The same cost hits a live
  keyframe: one 1280x960 image mask costs several seconds, which breaks the < 3 s keyframe->labels target.
- Decode time is proportional to mask pixels. The machine has 40 cores.

Fix it in our code (do not edit the installed library):
1. Decode each mask once: build the RLE once and derive the SVG path from that RLE (use the library's RLE->SVG
   conversion if it is reachable without re-decoding; otherwise convert RLE->SVG in our code), with a test that asserts
   one raster decode per mask beyond the parser's validation (count calls with a wrapper).
2. Send SAM smaller media: downscale keyframes and video clips to at most 640 px on the long side before the SAM call
   (ffmpeg for video, H.264, keep fps; Pillow only if it is already installed, otherwise ffmpeg for images too) and scale
   boxes/paths back to the original coordinates for overlays. Record the scale in the call record. SAM bills per
   image/frame, not per pixel, so cost does not change.
3. Take video mask conversion off the request path: return boxes and events right away, convert masks in a
   ProcessPoolExecutor (bounded, e.g. min(16, cpu_count)), and push overlays when ready (same pattern as the second
   opinion's WS diff). Cap overlay masks per clip to what the UI shows (e.g. every 3rd frame, at most 25 frames); boxes
   stay per frame.
4. Tests: keep the 75-frame live fixture, but have unit tests use a trimmed copy (first 3 frames, generated by a script
   you commit, checked into fixtures) and put the full-stream test behind a `slow` marker that CI still runs once.
Targets: full backend suite < 3 min; parsing + overlays for the 75-frame fixture < 25 s wall; one keyframe mask
decode < 1 s at 640 px. Measure before/after and put the numbers in docs/DECISIONS.md.
Run the backend suite (.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q), replay_check, and the Android build (offline, seeded
GRADLE_USER_HOME) until green. Do not commit. Finish with files changed, timings and test counts.
